icenter at time of quake</td><td>Overcast Clouds <img src=\"https://openweathermap.org/img/w/04d.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"50\" height=\"50\" /> <b>26.4°C</b> (79 F), humidity: 84%, wind: 7 m/s (13 kts) from S</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Estimated seismic energy released</td><td>2.5 x 10<sup>8</sup> joules (69.8 kilowatt hours) | equivalent to <b>ONE quake</b> of magnitude 2.4 | <a href=\"https://www.volcanodiscovery.com/earthquakes/energy.html\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">about seismic energy</a></td></tr>\n        </tbody></table>\n    \n\n    \n            \n            \n            <p>[smaller] [bigger]</p>\n\n        \n    \n    \n    \n\n    <h2>Nearby places</h2>The closest larger town near the epicenter is <a href=\"https://www.volcanodiscovery.com/place/360377/earthquakes/yonakuni.html\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Yonakuni</a>, a town with 1,700 inhabitants in <a href=\"https://www.volcanodiscovery.com/earthquakes/japan.html\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Japan</a>, in 61 km (38 mi) distance to the north, but it is unlikely that the quake was felt there.\n\n\n    <table>\n        <thead>\n        <tr>\n            <th>Distance<img src=\"https://volcanodiscovery.de/fileadmin/voldis/png/map-icon72.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" /></th>\n            <th>Place</th>\n            <th>Max. shaking intensity(*)</th>\n            <th>Region</th>\n            <th>Country</th>\n        </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n        \n        <tr>\n            <td><strong>61 km</strong> (38 mi)<p>N of epicenter</p></td>\n            <td><b><a href=\"https://www.volcanodiscovery.com/place/360377/earthquakes/yonakuni.html\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Yonakuni</a></b><p>(pop: 1,680)</p></td>\n            <td><p><b>I</b>: Not felt</p></td>\n            <td><a href=\"https://www.volcanodis